  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Mount Coolidge</strong> rises to 5,971 feet in South Dakota. The Mount Coolidge Trail covers 11.8 miles round trip (out-and-back) with about 610 feet of elevation gain \u2014 gentle grades, but the mileage is what makes it a Hard outing.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>Most of the climbing comes early \u2014 the first half of the route does the bulk of the work before the grade eases.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=43.74543,-103.43906\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">43.74543, -103.43906</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 25 miles southwest of Rapid City, South Dakota. Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Late May through October is the main season. Snow and ice linger into spring and return early in fall at this latitude and elevation; in winter this becomes a different, more serious undertaking requiring traction devices and warm layers.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Hard rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 4.0 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Cicero Peak, Little Devil's Tower and Black Elk Peak \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
